WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.169
-You are here in studio!
-I'm here!

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:06.806
-This is the most energy
we've ever felt in the studio

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.876
since we got back to the studio.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:12.745
-You and I know
how to bring the energy.

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:16.049
-I mean, are you used to
now walking out every day?

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:18.218
I mean, from doing the show
every day,

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:20.119
like, you have an entrance
every day?

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:24.257
-Yes. And our director, Adam,
you know, he was like,

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:27.293
"If you want to change it up
and walk from somewhere else,

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.828
there are no rules,"
and I was like, "Got it.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:31.697
It really took you saying that
for me to realize that."

00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:33.699
Like, I would have done
the same thing every day.

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:36.503
I always wanted to end the show
a certain way

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:39.505
and I finally found that with,
like, this thing, doggy bag.

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:41.641
We'll see if it works
'cause you said it too.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:44.344
You try things, and some things
work and some things don't.

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:46.812
-What's doggy bag?

00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:48.481
-It's something to take
with you.

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:50.450
-Oh!
-Like at a restaurant.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.153
-Yes. Brilliant.
-I personally could live

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:56.422
a very happy life
if I was a personal curator.

00:00:56.422 --> 00:00:58.658
Like, just let me curate
for you.

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.860
-Yeah.
-And that's what doggy bag is.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:04.096
-Yeah. I feel like it's kind of
what your show is as well.

00:01:04.096 --> 00:01:06.466
-It is a mood board.
It is a curation.

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:10.903
-It's so very you because you go
like, "Yeah, today I want to --

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:12.371
I want to talk to --"

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:15.341
You've launched that --
That kid star is gigantic.

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:18.344
-Jonah! Jonah Larson,
who did our pilot,

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:19.745
which was not a pilot,
let's face it.

00:01:19.745 --> 00:01:21.147
It was an audition tape,

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:24.483
and he came in from Wisconsin
and did it with me.

00:01:24.483 --> 00:01:27.253
And so we were able to get
to know each other in person,

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:30.657
which was great, so when
the show got picked up for real,

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:32.191
he was one of
my first phone calls.

00:01:32.191 --> 00:01:33.125
I was like I meant what I said.

00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:35.027
-This kid has got
personality plus.

00:01:35.027 --> 00:01:38.631
He's a superstar.
But you have him.

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:43.702
Pilar, who, I mean, the chef.
-Pilar.

00:01:43.702 --> 00:01:46.573
Pilar Valdes --
she's this extraordinary chef

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:50.042
who I hope soon
everyone will know,

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:52.545
and she's changed our lives,
and she's self-taught and cool.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:55.582
-But every day you have someone
on the show where I go like,

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:58.117
"Ooh, that's someone
I've never heard of,"

00:01:58.117 --> 00:01:59.452
and now they're part
of my world,

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:01.720
and I love that
you're doing that.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:04.891
-I feel like it's --
it was such an opportunity

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:07.927
for me to -- again, that's
that curation of life.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:12.631
I'm, like, I have found these
wonderful people in my journey

00:02:12.631 --> 00:02:15.835
and if I could ever be
alongside of them,

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:17.837
then, really,
that's the whole point.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.672
It's not, like, me presenting.

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:23.276
It's I want to stand next to
this person because I've --

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:25.744
I feel like life is better
with them in it.

00:02:25.744 --> 00:02:27.280
-Do you like
doing the interviews?

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.448
-I love it.

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:31.216
-I think my favorite interview
that you did

00:02:31.216 --> 00:02:34.086
was with your ex,
with Tom Green.

00:02:34.086 --> 00:02:35.822
That was unbelievable.

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:40.392
-And that was -- There was
no questions prepared for that.

00:02:40.392 --> 00:02:44.163
I had an offline conversation
with him because we didn't want

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:46.832
it to be some bougie Hollywood
moment like,

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:49.101
"Let's reconnect in front
of the cameras."

00:02:49.101 --> 00:02:52.104
But that said,
I was, like, you know --

00:02:52.104 --> 00:02:56.075
the thing that I love about Tom
was he is one of

00:02:56.075 --> 00:03:00.412
the first people to have put
a camera on his life, you know,

00:03:00.412 --> 00:03:02.382
when it was
a giant, fat camcorder

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:05.685
and there were
no easy phones available.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.020
-Yeah, yeah.
-You know?

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.488
His stuff was on, like, VHS.

00:03:09.488 --> 00:03:11.624
I remember watching
his VHS tapes.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:16.963
And so it's what gave me
the idea, because I just said,

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:21.901
you know, "Gosh, would you want
to, you know, kind of reconnect?

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.703
I feel like it's been
a long time,

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:27.273
and I would just love
to honor what you did.

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:30.142
You broke down all these doors.
You are a pioneer.

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:32.344
And I would love
to talk about it

00:03:32.344 --> 00:03:34.981
and have it be an excuse for us
to say hello."

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:37.383
That's the tone.
I sent him a video.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:38.717
And then he sent me one back.

00:03:38.717 --> 00:03:41.454
And immediately
he made me laugh,

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.555
and that's like my kryptonite.
-That's him.

00:03:43.555 --> 00:03:45.023
-Laughter.
-It was fascinating.

00:03:45.023 --> 00:03:46.692
It was fascinating TV.

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:48.594
If you have not seen it,
go on YouTube

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:52.031
or thedrewbarrymoreshow.com
and check out this clip.

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:53.933
It was just good.

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:57.837
It was different.
It was fresh and it was raw.

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.572
And I thought
that was fascinating.

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:00.806
I loved it.

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:04.477
-That means a lot
coming from you because I think

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:07.647
we're some of the least
"gotcha"-type of people.

00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:09.548
-Yeah. No, no, no,
I don't do that at all.

00:04:09.548 --> 00:04:13.653
-And I don't like doing it
and I don't want it done to me

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:15.922
and it's just not my wheelhouse.

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:23.796
And I just wanted to have a lot
of dignity and a gentle moment.

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:27.199
And it was nice to hear from
some people saying like,

00:04:27.199 --> 00:04:29.902
"I'd like to have that with
someone from my past,"

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:32.138
you know, whether it was
a specific person.

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:34.974
A lot of people were talking
about how they'd like to have

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:38.577
that kind of exchange
from someone who, you know,

00:04:38.577 --> 00:04:41.280
they had a significant chapter
of their life with.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.782
-Yeah, I think that's probably
the thing about your show

00:04:43.782 --> 00:04:46.452
is that daytime different
than late night,

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:47.786
but you kind of want to spark

00:04:47.786 --> 00:04:50.022
a conversation
and keep that going.

00:04:50.022 --> 00:04:53.025
I mean, and you did it.

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:55.361
But you know what else you did
that I was so impressed

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:57.696
and I already told you
and Chris Miller.

00:04:57.696 --> 00:05:01.167
I go, "How did you do
the invisible chair?"

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:04.670
-The green screen.
-The "Star Trek" guest.

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:07.473
You did it. Dude, you hit
a home run with that.

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:08.641
That was such a good idea.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:09.842
Here's the idea.

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:12.578
So, Drew is like,
"Here's my first guest."

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:15.915
I think it was
Lucy Liu and Cameron Diaz maybe.

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:18.550
They come walking out,
they sit on a chair,

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:20.153
and we're in quarantine.

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:22.454
You go, "No, no, no."
What? They're in your --

00:05:22.454 --> 00:05:24.223
What? How is this happening?
-Yeah.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:25.625
-It was totally --
They were in L.A.

00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:27.392
Or Cameron was in L.A.
-Cameron was in L.A.

00:05:27.392 --> 00:05:29.394
Lucy was in the studio.
-That freaked me out.

00:05:29.394 --> 00:05:30.896
It was amazing.

00:05:30.896 --> 00:05:34.400
But Cameron walks out like
she's walking on your studio.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.101
It doesn't look like a puppet
or something.

00:05:36.101 --> 00:05:39.705
It looks like a human being.
It's brilliantly done.

00:05:39.705 --> 00:05:41.407
You know who gave you props?

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:42.708
I don't know if --
You probably saw this.

00:05:42.708 --> 00:05:46.078
Oprah. Oprah Winfrey gave you --
she did an interview.

00:05:46.078 --> 00:05:47.579
I know, yeah, exactly.
-I can't believe it!

00:05:47.579 --> 00:05:49.348
-Yeah, Oprah gave you --
That's when you know

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:50.850
you're doing well, right,

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.718
when Oprah's like,
"I saw what Drew Barrymore did

00:05:52.718 --> 00:05:54.020
and I wanted to do that."

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.789
-I mean, just -- You know?
-Not bad.

00:05:56.789 --> 00:06:00.426
-But I'm glad because now
we can all embrace this.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:03.295
I mean, it's, like,
we're here on this show

00:06:03.295 --> 00:06:04.463
and it's a big deal now.

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:06.465
This used to be so status quo.

00:06:06.465 --> 00:06:08.233
No one thought about this.
-No.

00:06:08.233 --> 00:06:11.069
-And now to have a live person?
Some people --

00:06:11.069 --> 00:06:12.371
-We're so happy to have you.
[ Applause ]

00:06:12.371 --> 00:06:14.740
-It's a big deal!
-It's a giant deal.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:17.943
-It makes us appreciate it.
-I am so appreciative.

00:06:17.943 --> 00:06:19.178
You brought us a clip.

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:21.146
Here's a look at
"The Drew Barrymore Show."

00:06:21.146 --> 00:06:22.814
Take a look at this.

00:06:22.814 --> 00:06:24.817
-For anyone watching,

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:28.020
can you guess which one of us
isn't really here?

00:06:30.622 --> 00:06:33.292
-[ Gasps ]

00:06:33.292 --> 00:06:34.961
-Welcome back!

00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:37.863
-I'm the one in Los Angeles.

00:06:37.863 --> 00:06:41.067
-Oh!
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:43.669
-You got to try this.
It's so incredible.

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:46.371
The ether, the little particles
going out into space

00:06:46.371 --> 00:06:50.075
and coming back and remassing
into this beautiful space.

00:06:50.075 --> 00:06:51.910
You guys, it's crazy.
You should try it.

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:54.012
It tingles.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:54.012 --> 00:06:55.715
-It tingles. You got to try it.

00:06:55.715 --> 00:06:58.083
"The Drew Barrymore Show"
airs weekdays.

00:06:58.083 --> 00:07:00.319
Check your local listings or go

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:03.689
to thedrewbarrymoreshow.com
for more info.

